      "hf_completion": "To understand the difference, imagine you are teaching a child how to identify different types of fruit.\n\n### 1. Supervised Learning (The Teacher Method)\nIn supervised learning, you act as a teacher. You show the child a picture of an apple and say, **\"This is an apple.\"** Then you show them a banana and say, **\"This is a banana.\"**\n\nYou are providing the child with both the **data** (the picture) and the **answer** (the label).\n\n*   **How it works:** The computer is given a dataset where the \"right answers\" are already provided",
